1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:04,080
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,201
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:07,720
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,897
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,400
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:15,677
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:16,800
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,297
We came to this new world believing.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,977
That surely someday we
just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,180
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,897
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,957
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,160
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:37,880
I'm sorry, but we need
you to help find our kids.

54
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,897
They all went missing three years ago,

55
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:42,862
and not one of us has ever
heard from them again.

56
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,760
Please keep looking.

57
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,137
How could they have been lost at sea?

58
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:50,597
They were out playing in the
neighborhood when they disappeared.

59
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,500
It just doesn't make sense.

60
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:55,720
I beg you, please look for them again.

61
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,460
Just one more time.

62
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,061
Is Captain Toshiki here with you?

63
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,800
Can we at least go talk to her? Oh, yeah.

64
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,697
People say she really cares
a lot about our problems.

65
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:06,610
Please, sir.

66
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,497
Where's Captain Toshiki?

67
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,477
We need her help.

68
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,501
We're desperate.

69
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:11,910
Where is he?

70
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:14,460
Please, you have to... No!

71
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,660
This is too insulting.

72
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,557
We're no less a part of the G5
than Captain Toshiki, you know.

73
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:24,717
Not only do you doubt the Navy's report,

74
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:28,297
but then you have the goal to try and
tell us how we're supposed to do our jobs.

75
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,357
when we've been sent here to protect you?

76
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,500
I think you protest too much!

77
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,820
It's not like that. Shut up!

78
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,400
Too little, too late!

79
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,057
You might as well accept it.

80
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:39,460
Your kids are dead.

81
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:41,034
They were lost at sea!

82
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,040
It's over!

83
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,920
Ha! Take that!

84
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:57,120
Several times, too many to count, I discussed
it with Vergo, the G5's vice-admiral,

85
00:03:57,340 --> 00:04:00,660
and each investigation
came to nothing! What, sir?

86
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:03,217
Now just stay out of my way,

87
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:07,137
or I'll kill every last one of you and
burn this whole city to the ground!

88
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,867
Is that clear enough for ya?

89
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,500
Too clear, Commodore Yarisugi!

90
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,580
You wanna talk to Tashigi, eh?

91
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,280
Don't get too excited!

92
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:22,277
It'd sure be nice if I
could talk to her any time!

93
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,380
Too nice!

94
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:27,540
There he goes again!

95
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:35,320
But, unfortunately, Tashigi is the right
hand of Admiral Smoker in Unit 1! It's sad!

96
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,350
Too sad!

97
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:45,966
She can't help fools like you
with a case from three years ago!

98
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,480
She's a very busy lady!

99
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,800
Too busy!

100
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,517
Too busy!

101
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,280
Now piss off!

102
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:54,500
Too harsh!

103
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,377
There's no way he'll ever listen.

104
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,757
Do you think he was telling
us the truth when he said

105
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,237
he already tried to get help
from Vice Admiral Vergo,

106
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,150
though?

107
00:05:02,233 --> 00:05:06,407
I don't know about all that, but Vergo
did save this place from pirates before.

108
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,337
He seemed like such a gentleman.

109
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:11,640
I never would have guessed
that he was part of the G5.

110
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:14,907
So Vergo thinks they
were killed at sea, too.

111
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:17,780
They're still alive!

112
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,940
Our children are out there.

113
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,700
I can feel it.

114
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,900
But where in the world could they be?

115
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:42,800
I feel like I'm going to die.

116
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:45,237
Yusuf, quick, make them sleep.

117
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:48,520
I can, but it's only going
to work so many times.

118
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:51,160
Grown-ups, help us!

119
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,600
Please let us go!

120
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,400
Uh-oh,

121
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,257
I guess the withdrawals
from the drugs they've

122
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,297
been taking are causing
them a lot of pain.

123
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,733
So how do we help them?

124
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,840
You gotta do something, Sanji!

125
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,760
Uh, Sanji?

126
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,100
I'm Nami! Right, I forgot.

127
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,540
Aw, too bad.

128
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,717
Sanji's face looks so dependable.

129
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,900
I'm so sorry!

130
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,260
We need our candy.

131
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,237
Can we have some?

132
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,240
I can't eat candy!

133
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,280
Give it here!

134
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:31,460
We won't feel better without candy!

135
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:32,860
Candy!

136
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,800
Candy! Candy! Candy!

137
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,440
Get me! Right now!

138
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:41,800
Nobby!

139
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,580
Are you sure we can't hit them?

140
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:45,917
They're getting violent!

141
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,260
Don't you dare come on. They're just kids

142
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:55,846
Yeah, but we can't keep dodging
their attacks like this forever

143
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:19,860
You poor children.

144
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:21,611
You're not hurt, are you?

145
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,602
Let's go back to the laboratory.

146
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,960
It's not safe here.

147
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,757
Master! Master!

148
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:30,670
Master!

149
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:32,650
Master!

150
00:07:32,733 --> 00:07:33,563
Master!

151
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,360
Oh, dear!

152
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,362
Now it's angry!

153
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,974
I wonder what changed.

154
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,157
I'm going to venture a guess
here and say it's because

155
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:45,217
somebody decided to blow up
all the little baby slimeballs.

156
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,860
So that one is the parent?

157
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,042
Either way, there was no choice.

158
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:57,680
Hey, look.

159
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,540
I think it's transforming.

160
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,440
My word!

161
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,000
What a hideous beast!

162
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,960
It's a frog now?

163
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,060
I think it's a lizard.

164
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,630
Run!

165
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:50,097
Is it able to produce
unlimited copies of itself?

166
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:52,357
Actually, I don't think it's unlimited.

167
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,440
The one on that side is shrinking.

168
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:55,657
If that's the case,

169
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:59,317
then the other one should run out
of mass soon, but what's the point?

170
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:02,929
Wait, maybe it's trying to fling
itself over here in pieces.

171
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,397
We can't have it running
wild on this side.

172
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,837
People are going to get hurt.

173
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:14,897
Yeah, it spews gas when you cut
it and blows up when you burn it.

174
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:17,804
Plus, it's way bigger
than the ones from before.

175
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,700
The lab's in danger.

176
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:21,670
Let's hurry.

177
00:09:21,753 --> 00:09:22,583
Right.

178
00:09:22,666 --> 00:09:23,553
Time is of the essence.

179
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:25,290
Mamadouski!

180
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,817
I'm gonna head to the lab.

181
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,737
What do the rest of you plan to do?

182
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:32,157
Obviously, we're going to the lab, too,
since we have to stick together, stupid!

183
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,517
Who are you calling stupid?

184
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,657
Think about it, Mosshead.

185
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,857
If you wander off and get
separated from Kin'emon,

186
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:39,337
we're just gonna have to run all
over the island looking for you.

187
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,577
We don't have time for that!

188
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,131
There's no time for this.

189
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,420
Please stop arguing.

190
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,680
That's his thing!

191
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:51,139
I can't wait to see a real
hole, Samurai, in action.

192
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:52,960
To the laboratory, everyone!

193
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,960
Let Smokey go, Caesar!

194
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,800
And Captain Tashigi, too!

195
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:08,408
Damn, even a bazooka
won't break through it?

196
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,029
What's that thing made of?

197
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:11,338
How about the back?

198
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,977
There's no way in. I checked.

199
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,707
He's got to lock down tight.

200
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,624
Of course he does, the gas bag.

201
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:22,714
Hey, if we're stuck out here, then
we're all going to be killed for sure.

202
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,050
Huh?

203
00:10:24,133 --> 00:10:25,520
Don't say that. We'll make it.

204
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:26,680
I don't think so.

205
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:30,537
Those creepy slime things may
have stopped falling from the sky.

206
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:34,620
But look, they're forming together
and getting really freaking huge.

207
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,620
We can't get to a ship.

208
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:43,137
Our passmen cut off.

209
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:45,180
They took our transponder snails!

210
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,860
We can't call out! Crap!

211
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:49,079
They've got us completely isolated!

212
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,900
What exactly is Caesar doing?

213
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,900
Well, I can't say I know the details.

214
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:02,197
But he did finally awaken
his beloved pet Smiley, so...

215
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:05,280
I assume he's planning some
sort of big experiment.

216
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,080
By the way, Vergo...

217
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:11,192
Did you have a steak for breakfast today?

218
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,117
Yes, it's my favorite.

219
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,477
How did you know you're wearing some?

220
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:19,100
Just a little—I'd like to get a

221
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,597
quick look at the experiment before I go.

222
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:28,637
So everyone outside will die, probably,
but don't worry—you're safe in here!

223
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:33,777
Hey, Virgo—those men out there, you
know, they're all g5 soldiers, right?

224
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:38,740
g5 soldiers right They're your soldiers
and you're leaving them to die.

225
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,000
Yeah, I guess so

226
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,140
How could you?

227
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:48,980
You know, it's hard to believe we've
got so many big names in one cell.

228
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,560
It's quite a view

229
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:51,970
You're right.

230
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:55,937
It's so funny Seeing you two
locked up together again.

231
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:56,850
Oh, yeah

232
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:59,817
Alabasta that was where
you guys caught me and

233
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:03,140
smokey that one time
remember quiet you dumbass

234
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:07,840
Stupid pirates, don't you realize
the gravity of the situation here?

235
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:08,820
So it's true.

236
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,420
I was right.

237
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,240
I'm so disgusted.

238
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:15,340
Yeah, it's the worst case scenario.

239
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,180
Makes me sick too.

240
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:20,188
Those news articles
weren't simple mistakes.

241
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,157
The reporters were deliberately
misled because someone

242
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:26,064
in G5 wanted those abduction
reports covered up.

243
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,377
So they worked together.

244
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:31,777
Caesar abducted those children and Vergo

245
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:35,017
passed all the incidents
of as accidents at sea.

246
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:39,720
Of all people, the leader of
the base was a double agent.

247
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:45,100
That may be characteristic of G5,
but it's a disgrace for the Navy!

248
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,680
How could you do this?

249
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,580
Wait, I'm lost, so he's a bad guy?

250
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,617
Indeed, I'm surprised.

251
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:58,112
That's right, though they
wouldn't really have noticed it.

252
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:03,581
It's not like he changed; he's been a traitor
since the day that he joined the navy.

253
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:09,017
In fact, Vergo is a pirate all this time,

254
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:15,137
but why he enlisted in the navy on Joker's
orders before he made a name for himself.

255
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:20,337
He started at the very bottom and spent
15 years rising through the ranks.

256
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:25,517
Joker couldn't ask for a more reliable
or convenient soldier to work for him;

257
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,597
it's true.

258
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,060
He works for Joker.

259
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,280
He has been from the beginning.

260
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:31,770
Vergo!

261
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,140
Joker, huh? Hang on.

262
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:37,017
There's an underworld
broker by that name as well.

263
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,720
I was such an idiot.

264
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:42,937
How did I never smell a rat when
it was right there under my nose?

265
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:45,880
Aw, you shouldn't beat
yourself up like that.

266
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,270
Instead,

267
00:13:47,353 --> 00:13:51,257
you should commend the rat for being clever
enough to elude the great white hunter,

268
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:52,170
Smoker.

269
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,917
Ever since the day you were
transferred in from headquarters,

270
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,697
I've been on constant high alert.

271
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:58,957
And it's irritating;

272
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:03,140
I'm so relieved I won't have to
keep my head on a swivel anymore.

273
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:07,137
I've been in control of the
situation for a while now;

274
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:09,637
I'm sure they won't suspect me.

275
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:14,177
And besides, on the off chance
that they do find out about this,

276
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:16,880
I already know what I'm going to do.

277
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,040
I plan to.

278
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:22,980
Well, I assume you can figure that out.

279
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,920
Now then, Vice Admiral, Captain Tashigi.

280
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:34,400
You two will die here.

281
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:37,860
That way my secret never leaves this room.

282
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:41,580
I'll let Caesar handle
the soldiers outside.

283
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,440
It had to be done.

284
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:47,160
This territory belongs to Joker.

285
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:51,499
I can't allow anyone to walk out of
here knowing his identity, can I?

286
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:57,560
And yes, I'll report your deaths
as mere accident, as I always do.

287
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:58,930
Damn you.

288
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:03,740
Uh, hey, who's this Joker?

289
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:11,900
Well, I know Vergo because I know Joker.

290
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,137
Yeah, I worked for him.

291
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:19,396
Joker is just a fake name
he uses on the black market.

292
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:22,737
You know him.

293
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:24,702
In fact, you know him very well.

294
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,560
Who is he? Tell us.

295
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,291
One of the deadliest pirates in the world.

296
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:36,154
He is a member of the Seven Warlords,
authorized by the world government.

297
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:48,280
Don Quixote, Doflamingo.

298
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:03,880
Master!

299
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,624
You're the bastard who
kidnapped these children!

300
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,724
He shouldn't be here right now.

301
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,637
That means something bad must
have happened to Luffy's team.

302
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,280
You should be ashamed.

303
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,936
How could you do such a horrid thing?

304
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,120
Excuse me?

305
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,857
The children are suffering.

306
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:24,520
Why would you take them away
from my warm, safe lab? What?

307
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:25,740
No fighting!

308
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,937
We're not in a good place right now.

309
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:30,437
Maybe because you were holding
them against their will?

310
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:33,757
This guy's got a bounty of
300 million and Lock powers.

311
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,487
We're way out of our league!

312
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:40,777
I don't know what awful things you're
plotting here, and I don't care either.

313
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:43,617
These children told me
they wanted to go home.

314
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:46,397
I can't even imagine what their
parents are going through right now.

315
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:49,377
So mark my words—we are
getting them far away from you!

316
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:50,290
Let's

317
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:56,377
ask the children what they
really want, shall we?

318
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,290
we

319
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,440
Wait, hamster!

320
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:01,640
Hold on a sec!

321
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,035
He's a bad guy, okay?

322
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:06,279
He's gonna put you in that
lab and never let you go!

323
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,560
Outta my way!

324
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:13,650
Loose up!

325
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:18,660
There you go.

326
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:20,460
Come along, children.

327
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,157
I'll take good care of you.

328
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,897
Don't listen to a word he says!

329
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:25,451
He's trying to trick you!

330
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:28,369
Don't you want to go home?

331
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,560
Don't touch me!

332
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:39,860
There's bugs!

333
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:42,040
They're everywhere!

334
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:48,630
Nami!

335
00:17:48,713 --> 00:17:49,543
You alright?

336
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,020
Um, uh-huh.

337
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,280
Sorry, you left me with no choice!

338
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,330
Stop, no!

339
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:55,900
Stop it!

340
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,740
We can't let it go on like this, damn it!

341
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:00,297
The kid's hallucinating!

342
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,380
He thinks there's bugs everywhere!

343
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:04,120
I know, but...

344
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,214
You can't turn your weapon on a victim!

345
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,773
This isn't their fault!

346
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,180
Take these chains off!

347
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,280
You're hurting me!

348
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:21,657
We've got to do something about this!

349
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:24,017
These kids are gonna flip
out and smash us to pieces!

350
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:28,937
We're not getting anything
done till we stop him.

351
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:36,020
Good

352
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,397
children,

353
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:48,657
look how powerful you've
become—that bastard!

354
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:50,817
We need it.

355
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:51,730
it

356
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,080
Master, give it.

357
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,440
That's enough.

358
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:57,721
You're finished.

359
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,900
This one should work well against gas.

360
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:05,420
Special attack, Firebird Star!

361
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:10,180
Moving, kids, watch out!

362
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:15,670
Huh?

363
00:19:15,820 --> 00:19:17,996
Did you think I would simply explode?

364
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,920
Your understanding of science is flawed.

365
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:22,570
Pay attention,

366
00:19:22,653 --> 00:19:25,457
I can put out a fire
long before it reaches

367
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:28,440
me because poison gas isn't the only kind.

368
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:32,097
The oxygen all around us is gas as well,

369
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:37,697
and what that means is that I can control
the nearby air with the greatest of ease.

370
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:40,957
Your fire died out when I
removed the oxygen around me.

371
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:44,452
Why don't we see what happens
when I remove yours as well?

372
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:51,740
Just like this!

373
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,620
Hang in there!

374
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,620
Black Ball!

375
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:10,700
Doorclad!

376
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:15,050
Ah!

377
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:21,350
Master!

378
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,090
Please!

379
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:27,590
Candy!

380
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:28,990
Candy!

381
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:32,340
Ah yes!

382
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:36,624
Since I'm here, you're likely
wondering if Straw Hat ran into me.

383
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:38,760
Indeed he did.

384
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:41,560
Along with two other friends of yours.

385
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:45,220
I made them suffocate just like you.

386
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:46,850
Esther!

387
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:48,390
Hurry!

388
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:49,690
Candy!

389
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:51,860
I can't wait!

390
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:04,800
Listen up, children.

391
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,513
I have plenty of candy,

392
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:11,012
but I'm only giving it to the good boys
and girls who come back to the lab.

393
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,920
I'll be very good.

394
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:15,740
Can you behave just a little while longer?

395
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,320
We'll go back, but hurry.

396
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:21,200
Yes, yes, soon enough.

397
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,560
Just one last thing.

398
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:27,533
The people who tried to take
you away are very, very bad.

399
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:31,778
And because they hurt you so much,
I'm going to need you to kill them.

400
00:21:37,980 --> 00:21:43,020
Just grab a pipe or a big rock
and crush their miserable skulls!

401
00:21:50,380 --> 00:21:52,220
No! Stop!

402
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,920
I can't hope!

403
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,920
I'm flicking out!

404
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:05,870
Caesar!

405
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:09,310
Caesar!

406
00:22:09,393 --> 00:22:10,223
Yeah!

407
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:23,980
It's brown bear!

408
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:25,417
That's close, but no.

409
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:27,000
Forgive me, Straw Hat!

410
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:30,040
I finally see the truth!

411
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:36,220
Wait, who are you again?

412
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:40,760
Oh, yes, you're one of my
dutiful lackeys, aren't you?

413
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:43,000
Your name was, uh...

414
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:44,430
Brownbeard.

415
00:22:44,513 --> 00:22:46,987
Left me for dead and
forgot about me already?

416
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:52,240
I was only kidding, of course.

417
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,951
But what happened to you?

418
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:57,552
All those awful injuries, why
it looks like you were shot.

419
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,017
You can't fool me!

420
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:01,900
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID!

421
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,645
You're Brownbeard, aren't you?

422
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,380
Just so you know.

423
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:10,160
You happen to be on our hit list, too.

424
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:15,357
He's a fool, so it was easy to manipulate
him, but now he's become a nuisance.

425
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:18,440
I don't need his services
anymore. Kill him!

426
00:23:20,220 --> 00:23:21,660
The Cool Brothers.

427
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:28,020
Yes, I do recall asking a favor from them.

428
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:32,500
And all this time, I trusted you.

429
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:35,720
No reason to be mad.

430
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:41,097
I underestimated your worth, but
it's all water under the bridge now.

431
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:42,298
You're still alive.

432
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:45,100
Why, it seems everything is just dandy.

433
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:46,980
Shut your mouth!

434
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:51,140
I'll kill you!

435
00:23:56,520 --> 00:23:57,660
Careful, children!

436
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,380
It's dangerous here!

437
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:03,335
You'd better get aboard the
flying gas balloon outside.

438
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:05,120
I'll be with you shortly.

439
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:09,840
Please don't go!

440
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:11,374
We can still help you!

441
00:24:14,180 --> 00:24:15,010
Caesar!

442
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:21,220
It's my fault that you
tricked me. That's fine.

443
00:24:22,140 --> 00:24:24,700
I'll bear that suffering on my own.

444
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:30,837
But I won't let my crew go through
the same hell. Give them back.

445
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:33,600
I'm taking my men and leaving this place.

446
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,497
Huh, your men?

447
00:24:41,580 --> 00:24:43,780
There's no such thing. You fool.

448
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:49,457
If I recall every last one of you, pledged
your allegiance to me when you came here.

449
00:24:49,540 --> 00:24:51,497
You're not the captain
of anything anymore.

450
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:52,937
You're a failure.

451
00:24:53,020 --> 00:24:54,840
You'd all be dead without me.

452
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:57,320
Hey, Nami!

453
00:24:57,580 --> 00:24:59,420
Let's go after the kids! Right.

454
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:02,837
All the little fools who
couldn't make it in the

455
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:05,920
new world will keep
worshipping me as their savior.

456
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:08,437
They're not good for anything else.

457
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:12,697
I only keep them around as my guinea
pigs, just waiting for their turn to die.

458
00:25:12,780 --> 00:25:14,400
I'm gonna smash you!

459
00:25:29,220 --> 00:25:30,360
That looks bad.

460
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:31,893
Do you think he's okay?

461
00:25:41,260 --> 00:25:42,360
That's the nut!

462
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:48,280
Where did you go?

463
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,620
You said you'd be here.

464
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:54,100
Are you there, Monet?

465
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:55,670
Uh-huh.

466
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:58,388
I retrieved the children
without difficulty.

467
00:25:58,580 --> 00:26:01,260
Did you prepare Smiley's food, as I asked?

468
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:04,937
I followed your instructions to the
letter, so everything is in good order.

469
00:26:05,020 --> 00:26:05,920
As always.

470
00:26:07,820 --> 00:26:11,114
And the video transponder
snails are on standby outside.

471
00:26:11,540 --> 00:26:12,370
I see.

472
00:26:12,453 --> 00:26:15,000
So when my adorable little Smiley arrives,

473
00:26:15,220 --> 00:26:18,897
we can broadcast the experiment
for all of our associates to see?

474
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:19,810
Certainly.

475
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:22,750
Splendid.

476
00:26:22,833 --> 00:26:24,757
Connect me to all the receivers now.

477
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:25,860
Right away.

478
00:26:27,380 --> 00:26:30,560
A fun hello to all you
illicit brokers out there.

479
00:26:30,860 --> 00:26:33,240
I do apologize for the short notice.

480
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:36,799
But you're about to witness
something extraordinary.

481
00:26:37,740 --> 00:26:41,152
I've found the perfect opportunity
for this demonstration.

482
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:43,957
This is a poison gas
weapon I've developed,

483
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,177
much like the one you saw four years ago,

484
00:26:46,260 --> 00:26:49,777
but with some new features the
government could never hope to recreate.

485
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:54,566
At any rate, it just so happens that I
have some uninvited guests on the island.

486
00:26:54,900 --> 00:26:57,820
They're going to aid me
at my live test today.

487
00:27:03,060 --> 00:27:05,860
Intimidation, war, annihilation.

488
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,920
It has a variety of uses.

489
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:14,280
If it happens to tickle your fancy, I
would be more than happy to make a deal.

490
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:16,400
You can't stop us forever!

491
00:27:19,940 --> 00:27:22,200
Poison doesn't seem like your style.

492
00:27:22,700 --> 00:27:23,760
It's not.

493
00:27:26,220 --> 00:27:29,920
But hey, it never hurts to
watch a little carnage, does it?
